2026-10-17, pairing
- Sign-in is now pairing with the user's Warpnet node: a QR scan or pasted
  connection data replaces the instance picker and OAuth. AddAccountsView, the
  Apps and Oauth endpoints, the OAuth token and app models and the
  instances.social client were removed. The app keeps one pairing; AppAccount
  names the paired node, and logging out unpairs the device on that node.
- The Mastodon push stack went with OAuth, since every subscription was keyed
  by an OAuth token: PushNotificationsService, its settings screen, the
  IceCubesNotifications extension, the push endpoint and models, the
  aps-environment entitlement and the remote-notification background mode.
- The node is paused in the background and resumed in the foreground.
- Package manifests must start with their tools version, so they carry the
  notice line second.
